{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The 4+1 View Model"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about  architecture view models."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "\"Interpret the technical design report, to determine the work plan during the phase of building the software, based on regulation ad protocols established by the company.  Design the architecture design using the appropriate tools and types acccording to the software requirements. \""}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.   Recognizes simple ideas on persisting storage, web applications, and the functional phase of an IT project."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Quantifiers"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>You use <strong>quantifiers</strong>&nbsp;to give information about indefinite quantities.</p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I still don't understand plenty of things you've done there."}, {"type": "example", "content": "That's a lot of information to work with."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I think you've said enough."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p><strong>Quantifiers</strong> are always before the object they are modifying. You can use them with countable and uncountable nouns.</p> <p>Some <strong>quantifiers</strong> that go with countable nouns are <i>many,</i> <i>few</i>, and a <i>few</i>:</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Examples:</p> <p><i>There are <strong>many</strong> aspects in that diagram that I can&rsquo;t understand.</i></p> <p><i>For the last <strong>few </strong>years, software development has changed enough. </i></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Some quantifiers that go with uncountable nouns are <i>much, little,</i> and <i>a little</i>.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Examples:&nbsp;</p> <p><i>I think there is not <strong>much</strong> information in that diagram. </i></p> <p><i>There is probably very<strong> little</strong> chance of finishing the whole project in such as short term.</i></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>There are some <strong>quantifiers</strong> that either go before countable or uncountable nouns such as <i>some, a lot of, lots of, plenty of,</i> and <i>enough</i>.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>Examples:</p> <p><i>I have <strong>plenty of </strong>ideas for our software project.</i></p> <p><i>She is doing <strong>a lot of</strong> effort to finish the presentation. </i></p> <p><i>He thinks he doesn&rsquo;t have <strong>enough</strong> time to prepare the process review. </i></p>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "What is a view model?"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>A <strong>view model</strong> is the representation of a system from a specific perspective.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>You use <strong>view models</strong> or viewpoint frameworks to represent the whole system in views that will help the stakeholders, end users, developers, managers and testers among others, to understand the system from different perspectives depending on the specific concern, such concern can be security, processes or development.</p> <p>Among the many <strong>view models</strong>, one of the most important and common ones is the 4+1 view model, it allows the stakeholders to see the system from 4 different views and an extra one that permits to analyze all the 4 views once they are completed.</p>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "piping diagram"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a diagram that shows the interconnection between processes"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's just a piping diagram to explain how, where and what the program, I've just designed for the company, is doing."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "baffled"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "perplex or puzzled about something  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm kind of baffled by what you've said."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob11aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "step by step"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "one at a time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(idiom)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The second view is the process view, which describes step by step the relation each activity has within the system."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob11aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "relate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to understand a situation"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: As you can relate, it describes the mapping of software onto hardware. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob11aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mapping"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the action of relating and linking objects into one set"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It describes the mapping of software onto hardware and the distribution aspects. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob11aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "station"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a server that is always broadcasting "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's like having a computer or a server working only one function of all the software and the relation between that station with the others."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob11aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for more information about the use of the 4+1 view model in a company."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Imagine that you have any kind of Software Company."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a brochure explaining the implementation of the 4 views on your fictitious company.   "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your brochure with your classmates. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research about the four views of a 4+1 view model."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create an imaginary software company."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I design a brochure to explain the use of the 4+1 model views in a company and I show my ideas to classmates and discuss them. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain what an architecture view model is. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the 4+1 View Model. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can describe the four views the 4+1 model provides. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What kind of diagrams do you know?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What would you use a diagram for in software architecture?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attem